      "text": "The researchers developed a method called high-fold homogeneous expansion microscopy. They reported about eight- to nine-fold expansion in a single round and tested structural preservation in centrioles and nuclear pore complexes. The method also supports labeling after expansion. The main point is to check both how much a sample expands and how well its structure is preserved.",
